{"paper": "2024-Tier1-11-Sep-2024-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 25, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Naman bought few apples for ₹720 from a shop. He negotiated the price and the shopkeeper reduced it by ₹2 per apple. Due to this Naman could buy four more apples than what he had bought earlier. How many apples did he originally buy?", "options": [{"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "The tank is filled by three pipes with different uniform flow rates. While the first two pipes are operating simultaneously, they fill the tank in the same duration that the third pipe takes to fill it alone. The second pipe can fill the tank 5 hours quicker than the first pipe, yet 4 hours slower than the third pipe. What is the time (in hours) needed for the first pipe to fill the tank?", "options": [{"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "9", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Sohan borrows a sum of ₹1,41,545 at the rate of 11% per annum simple interest. At the end of the first year, he repays ₹25,490 towards return of principal amount borrowed. If Sohan clears all pending dues at the end of the second year, including interest payment that accrued during the first year, how much does he pay (in ₹) at the end of the second year?", "options": [{"text": "1,44,391", "added": false}, {"text": "1,36,453", "added": false}, {"text": "1,41,222", "added": false}, {"text": "1,37,407", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "The table given here represents the distance (in km) travelled by two athletes X and Y in the same direction. Y’s average speed (km/hour) during the first five hours is:", "options": [{"text": "33", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Express sin 74° + tan 74° in terms of trigonometric ratios of angles between 0° and 45°.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "complementary-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A cuboid of dimensions 50 cm, 150 cm, 175 cm can be divided into how many identical largest cubes?", "options": [{"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "84", "added": false}, {"text": "85", "added": false}, {"text": "90", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1471 : 1367", "added": false}, {"text": "1230 : 1331", "added": false}, {"text": "1367 : 1471", "added": false}, {"text": "1331 : 1230", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "If Ram purchases a fan, he gets 8% discount, however, if he purchases three fans he gets 6% on the first, 10% on the second and 12% on the third. If the price paid by the Ram for three fans is ₹6,800, then what will be the marked price of each fan?", "options": [{"text": "₹2,400", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,450", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,550", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "A boat can go 54 km upstream in 6 hours. If the speed of the stream is 4.8 km/h, then how much time (in hours) will the boat take to cover a distance of 279 km downstream?", "options": [{"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "P and Q are centres of two circles whose radii are 7 cm and 3 cm, respectively. If the direct common tangents to the circles meet PQ extended at A, then A divides PQ _________.", "options": [{"text": "externally in the ratio 3 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "internally in the ratio 3 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "externally in the ratio 7 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "internally in the ratio 7 : 3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Consider the given table for total imports of goods of 5 companies over 5 years (in lakhs), and answer the question that follows. If the total exports of all companies together in the year 2013 is ₹300 lakh, then the profit/loss of all companies together in year 2013 is: (Assume: Profit = Exports – Imports)", "options": [{"text": "loss of ₹27 lakh", "added": false}, {"text": "loss of ₹18 lakh", "added": false}, {"text": "profit of ₹30 lakh", "added": false}, {"text": "profit of ₹35 lakh", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "63", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "42,150", "added": false}, {"text": "43,250", "added": false}, {"text": "40,150", "added": false}, {"text": "41,250", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "87", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "77", "added": false}, {"text": "79", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "A class of 30 students appeared in a test. The average score of 12 students is 62, and that of the rest is 74. What is the average score of the class?", "options": [{"text": "70.2", "added": false}, {"text": "69.2", "added": false}, {"text": "68.2", "added": false}, {"text": "67.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "-1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "other", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "What is the ratio of the mean proportional of 1.21 and 0.09 with the mean proportional of 0.16 and 0.36?", "options": [{"text": "11 : 8", "added": false}, {"text": "13 : 8", "added": false}, {"text": "13 : 12", "added": false}, {"text": "11 : 13", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Replace * by the smallest digit so that 723*56* is divisible by 6.", "options": [{"tex